<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Expanding a binomial by multiplication</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Expand \({@brn@}\) by multiplying out brackets. Collect like terms.</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\({@brn@}\) means \({@n@}\) factors of \(({@br@})\) multiplied together, never \({@fresh@}\). Multiply two brackets, collect like terms, then multiply by the next bracket.</p><p>First, \(({@br@})^2 = {@sq@}\). Multiply this by \(({@br@})\):</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\(\times\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@x^2@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@t2@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@b2@}\)</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@x@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(x)*(x^2)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(x)*(t2)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(x)*(b2)@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@b@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(b)*(x^2)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(b)*(t2)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(b)*(b2)@}\)</td></tr></table><p>Collecting like terms, \(({@br@})^3 = {@cu@}\).</p>[[if test="is(n=4)"]]<p>Multiply by \(({@br@})\) once more:</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\(\times\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@x^3@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@t3@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@t4@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@b3@}\)</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@x@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(x)*(x^3)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(x)*(t3)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(x)*(t4)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(x)*(b3)@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@b@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(b)*(x^3)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(b)*(t3)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(b)*(t4)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@(b)*(b3)@}\)</td></tr></table><p>Collecting like terms, \(({@br@})^4 = {@ta@}\).</p>[[/if]]<p>The coefficients come from the row {@crow@}. Check: putting \(x = 1\) gives \({@(1+b)@}^{@n@} = {@chk@}\) on both sides.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
