  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Binomial Expansions: expanding by multiplication</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 1.2: Expand a power of a binomial (x + b)^n, n = 3 or 4, by multiplying out brackets.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 5, Section A, Exercise A, question 1 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 2 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: new expressions and powers, randomised; the expansion is done by repeated multiplication with a grid.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
